# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# homelab-ad-ds — .gitignore
#
# This repo is documentation + scripts only. Nothing here should ever be a
# large binary or a machine-local artifact. The rules below cover OS/editor
# cruft and, most importantly, VM media that would blow past GitHub's file
# size limits if it ever landed in this folder by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?

# --- Windows (the lab guest OS writes these onto shared folders) ---
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# --- Linux ---
.directory
.fuse_hidden*
.nfs*

# --- Editors / IDEs ---
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project
\#*\#
.\#*

# --- VM disk images & installation media -----------------------------------
# NEVER commit these. A single Windows Server ISO or qcow2 disk is multiple
# gigabytes; GitHub rejects files over 100 MB and warns above 50 MB. If one of
# these needs to be preserved, keep it outside the repo or on external storage.
*.iso
*.img
*.qcow2
*.qcow
*.vdi
*.vmdk
*.vhd
*.vhdx
*.ova
*.ovf
*.utm/
*.utm

# --- Archives (usually ISO/driver bundles in disguise) ---
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# --- Logs, dumps, and exports ---
*.log
*.etl
*.dmp
*.evtx

# --- Secrets: credentials must never be committed to a portfolio repo ------
# Lab passwords (DSRM, domain admin) belong in a password manager, not git.
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.cer
credentials.txt
secrets.*
.env
.env.*
